{"title": "3D Mensuration 3 (Past Year Questions)", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A solid cone of radius 7 cm and height 7 cm was melted along with two solid spheres of radius 7 cm each to form a solid cylinder of radius 7 cm. what is the curved surface area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of the cylinder?</p><p>(user&#960; = 22/7)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 7cm &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 7cm &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; 7cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 7cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>(&#960; = 22/7 &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;)</p>", "options_en": ["2196", "924", "482", "880"], "options_hi": ["2196", "924", "482", "880"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of cone + volume of 2 spheres = volume of cylinder </p><p>1/3 * &#960; * 7<sup>2 </sup>* 7 + 2 * 4/3 * &#960; * 7<sup>3</sup> = &#960; * 7<sup>2 </sup>* height of cylinder </p><p>7/3 + 56/3 = height of cylinder </p><p>Height of cylinder = 21 cm</p><p>Therefore, curved surface area of cylinder = 2 * 22/7 * 7 * 21 = 924 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of cone + volume of 2 spheres = volume of cylinder </p><p>1/3 * &#960; * 7<sup>2 </sup>* 7 + 2 * 4/3 * &#960; * 7<sup>3</sup> = &#960; * 7<sup>2 </sup>* height of cylinder </p><p>7/3 + 56/3 = height of cylinder </p><p>Height of cylinder = 21 cm</p><p>Therefore, curved surface area of cylinder = 2 * 22/7 * 7 * 21 = 924 cm<sup>2</sup></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A spherical box has surface area 528 cm<sup>2</sup>. Find the radius of the spherical box.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 528 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&radic;37 cm", "&radic;42 cm", "&radic;29 cm", "&radic;35 cm"], "options_hi": ["&radic;37 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "&radic;42 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "&radic;29 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "&radic;35 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Surface area of spherical box = 528 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>4 * 22/7 * r<sup>2</sup> = 528</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 528*7/88</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 42</p><p>r = &radic;42 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Surface area of spherical box = 528 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>4 * 22/7 * r<sup>2</sup> = 528</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 528*7/88</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 42</p><p>r = &radic;42 cm</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The cost of painting a spherical vessel of diameter 14 cm is &#8377; 21,560. What is the cost of painting (in &#8377;) per square centimetre? (Use &#960; = 22/7)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#8377;21,560 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#8377; = 22/7 &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;)</p>", "options_en": ["30", "32", "28", "35"], "options_hi": ["30", "32", "28", "35"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Radius of spherical vessel = 14/2 = 7 cm</p><p>Surface area of spherical vessel = 4&#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 4 * 22/7 * 7<sup>2</sup> = 616 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Total cost = &#8377; 21560</p><p>Cost per cm<sup>2</sup> = 21560/616 = &#8377;35</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Radius of spherical vessel = 14/2 = 7 cm</p><p>Surface area of spherical vessel = 4&#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 4 * 22/7 * 7<sup>2</sup> = 616 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Total cost = &#8377; 21560</p><p>Cost per cm<sup>2</sup> = 21560/616 = &#8377;35</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of the total surface area and volume of a sphere is 2 : 7. Its radius is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 2 : 7 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["10.5 cm", "7 cm", "10 cm", "7.5 cm"], "options_hi": ["10.5 cm", "7 cm", "10 cm", "7.5 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the radius of sphere = R cm</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>4&#960;R<sup>2</sup>: 4&#960;R<sup>3</sup>/3 = 2: 7</p><p>3/R = 2/7</p><p>R = 10.5 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the radius of sphere = R cm</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>4&#960;R<sup>2</sup>: 4&#960;R<sup>3</sup>/3 = 2: 7</p><p>3/R = 2/7</p><p>R = 10.5 cm</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>One laddoo with a radius of 5 cm belongs to a shopkeeper. How many laddoos of radius 2.5 cm may be created from the same one laddoo?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2337;&#2381;&#2337;&#2370; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2354;&#2337;&#2381;&#2337;&#2370; &#2360;&#2375; 2.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2337;&#2381;&#2337;&#2370; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["2", "6", "4", "8"], "options_hi": ["2", "6", "4", "8"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Radius of large laddoo = 5 cm</p><p>Volume of large laddoo = 4/3 &#960; * 5<sup>3</sup></p><p>Radius of small laddoo = 2.5 cm</p><p>Volume of small laddoo = 4/3 &#960; * (2.5)<sup>3</sup></p><p>Number of small laddoos = [4/3 &#960; * 5<sup>3</sup>]/[ 4/3 &#960; * 2.5<sup>3</sup>] = (5/2.5)<sup>3</sup> = 8</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Radius of large laddoo = 5 cm</p><p>Volume of large laddoo = 4/3 &#960; * 5<sup>3</sup></p><p>Radius of small laddoo = 2.5 cm</p><p>Volume of small laddoo = 4/3 &#960; * (2.5)<sup>3</sup></p><p>Number of small laddoos = [4/3 &#960; * 5<sup>3</sup>]/[ 4/3 &#960; * 2.5<sup>3</sup>] = (5/2.5)<sup>3</sup> = 8</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the volume of a sphere is equal to that of a cylinder having the same radius, then find the ratio of the radius to height of the cylinder.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344;, &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1 : 2", "2 : 3", "3 : 4", "3 : 5"], "options_hi": ["1 : 2", "2 : 3", "3 : 4", "3 : 5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the radius of cylinder = radius of sphere = r </p><p>Let height of cylinder = h</p><p>Then, volume of sphere = volume of cylinder </p><p>4/3 * &#960; * r<sup>3</sup> = &#960; * r<sup>2</sup> * h </p><p>r: h = 3: 4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the radius of cylinder = radius of sphere = r </p><p>Let height of cylinder = h</p><p>Then, volume of sphere = volume of cylinder </p><p>4/3 * &#960; * r<sup>3</sup> = &#960; * r<sup>2</sup> * h </p><p>r: h = 3: 4</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The radius of a hemispherical bowl is 9 cm. The capacity of the bowl is: (Use &#960; = 22/7)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2350;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;: (&#960; = 22/7 &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;)</p>", "options_en": ["1527.43 cm<sup>3</sup>", "1428.78 cm<sup>3</sup>", "1625.37 cm<sup>3</sup>", "1821.47 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["1527.43 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "1428.78 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "1625.37 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "1821.47 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Radius = 9 cm</p><p>Volume of hemispherical bowl = 2/3 * 22/7 * 9<sup>3</sup> = 44 * 729/21 &#8776; 1527.43 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Radius = 9 cm</p><p>Volume of hemispherical bowl = 2/3 * 22/7 * 9<sup>3</sup> = 44 * 729/21 &#8776; 1527.43 cm<sup>3</sup></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A solid lead sphere of radius 11 cm is melted and recast into small solid spheres of radius 2 cm each. How many maximum numbers (in integer) of such spheres can be made?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>11 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2360;&#2368;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 2 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2369;&#2344;&#2307; &#2338;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; (&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2379; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["125", "166", "100", "30"], "options_hi": ["125", "166", "100", "30"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>The volume of a sphere = 4/3 &#960;r<sup>3</sup></p><p>The volume of the sphere of radius of 11 cm = 4/3 &#960; * 11<sup>3</sup></p><p>The volume of one sphere of radius of 2 cm = 4/3 &#960; * 2<sup>3</sup></p><p>The maximum number of small spheres, which can be made = 4/3 &#960; * 11<sup>3</sup>/4/3 &#960; * 2<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 1331/8</p><p>= 166 (Approx.)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The volume of a sphere = 4/3 &#960;r<sup>3</sup></p><p>The volume of the sphere of radius of 11 cm = 4/3 &#960; * 11<sup>3</sup></p><p>The volume of one sphere of radius of 2 cm = 4/3 &#960; * 2<sup>3</sup></p><p>The maximum number of small spheres, which can be made = 4/3 &#960; * 11<sup>3</sup>/4/3 &#960; * 2<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 1331/8</p><p>= 166 (Approx.)</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A hemispherical bowl is 88 cm round the brim. Assuming it to be full, how many persons may be served from it in hemispherical glasses, 7 cm in diameter at the top? (Where &#960; = 22/7)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 88 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2361; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2351;&#2361; &#2349;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2311;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2327;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352;&#2379;&#2360;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; 7 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#960; = 22/7)</p>", "options_en": ["74", "68", "64", "70"], "options_hi": ["74", "68", "64", "70"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Circumference of hemispherical bowl = 2&#960;r = 88 cm</p><p>2  X  (22/7)  X  r = 88</p><p>r = 88  X  7/44 </p><p>r = 14 cm</p><p>Radius of hemispherical bowl = 7/2 = 3.5 cm</p><p>Number of glasses = (2/3 * &#960; * 14<sup>3</sup>) &div; (2/3 * &#960; * 3.5<sup>3</sup>)</p><p>= (14/3.5)<sup>3</sup> </p><p>= 64</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Circumference of hemispherical bowl = 2&#960;r = 88 cm</p><p>2  X  (22/7)  X  r = 88</p><p>r = 88  X  7/44 </p><p>r = 14 cm</p><p>Radius of hemispherical bowl = 7/2 = 3.5 cm</p><p>Number of glasses = (2/3 * &#960; * 14<sup>3</sup>) &div; (2/3 * &#960; * 3.5<sup>3</sup>)</p><p>= (14/3.5)<sup>3</sup> </p><p>= 64</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The curved surface area of the sphere is 154 cm<sup>2</sup>. Find the volume of the sphere (rounded off to one digit after decimal) .</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 154 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; (&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2340;&#2325;)&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["156.9 cm<sup>3</sup>", "179.7 cm<sup>3</sup>", "161.1 cm<sup>3</sup>", "147.8 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["156.9 cm<sup>3</sup>", "179.7 cm<sup>3</sup>", "161.1 cm<sup>3</sup>", "147.8 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Curved surface area of the sphere is 154 <img width=29 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image025.png\"></p><p>4&#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 154</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=55 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image026.png\"></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=24 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image027.png\"></p><p>r = <img width=15 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image028.png\">cm</p><p>Volume of the sphere =<img width=16 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image029.png\">&#960;r<sup>3</sup></p><p>= <img width=116 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image030.png\"></p><p>= 179.7 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Curved surface area of the sphere is 154 <img width=29 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image025.png\"></p><p>4&#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 154</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=55 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image026.png\"></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=24 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image027.png\"></p><p>r = <img width=15 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image028.png\">cm</p><p>Volume of the sphere =<img width=16 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image029.png\">&#960;r<sup>3</sup></p><p>= <img width=116 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image030.png\"></p><p>= 179.7 cm<sup>3</sup></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The volumes of two spheres are in the ratio of 512: 3375. The ratio of their surface areas is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 512: 3375 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["64:225", "49:325", "27:144", "68:125"], "options_hi": ["64:225", "49:325", "27:144", "68:125"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio of volumes of two spheres = 512:3375</p><p>(4&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>3</sup>/3)/(4&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>3</sup>/3) = 512/3375</p><p>r<sub>1</sub><sup>3</sup>/r<sub>2</sub><sup>3</sup> = (8/15)<sup>3</sup></p><p>r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub> = 8/15</p><p>Ratio of their surface areas = (4&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>)/(4&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>) </p><p>= (r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup> </p><p>= (8/15)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 64/225</p><p>= 64:225</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio of volumes of two spheres = 512:3375</p><p>(4&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>3</sup>/3)/(4&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>3</sup>/3) = 512/3375</p><p>r<sub>1</sub><sup>3</sup>/r<sub>2</sub><sup>3</sup> = (8/15)<sup>3</sup></p><p>r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub> = 8/15</p><p>Ratio of their surface areas = (4&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>)/(4&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>) </p><p>= (r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup> </p><p>= (8/15)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 64/225</p><p>= 64:225</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many spherical lead shots each of diameter 8.4 cm can be obtained from a rectangular solid of lead with dimension 88 cm, 63 cm, 42 cm (take &#960; = 22/7)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366; 88 cm, 63 cm, 42 cm (&#960; = 22/7 &#2354;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;) &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2368;&#2360;&#2375;/&#2354;&#2375;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2360;&#2375; 8.4 cm &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2375;&#2337; &#2358;&#2377;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["920", "750", "650", "860"], "options_hi": ["920", "750", "650", "860"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Diameter of spherical lead shots = 8.4 cm</p><p>Radius of spherical lead shots = 8.4/2 = 4.2 cm</p><p>Since volume of the object will remain constant.</p><p>Let 'n' number of lead balls can be obtained.</p><p>So, Volume of 'n' spherical balls = Volume of rectangular solid</p><p><img width=88 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image066.png\"></p><p><img width=176 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image067.png\"></p><p><img width=201 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image068.png\"></p><p><img width=145 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image069.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image070.png\"></p><p>n = 750</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Diameter of spherical lead shots = 8.4 cm</p><p>Radius of spherical lead shots = 8.4/2 = 4.2 cm</p><p>Since volume of the object will remain constant.</p><p>Let 'n' number of lead balls can be obtained.</p><p>So, Volume of 'n' spherical balls = Volume of rectangular solid</p><p><img width=88 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image066.png\"></p><p><img width=176 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image067.png\"></p><p><img width=201 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image068.png\"></p><p><img width=145 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image069.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image070.png\"></p><p>n = 750</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the radius of a sphere is increased by 125%, then by what percentage will its surface area increase (correct to two decimal places)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 125% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366; (&#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325;)?</p>", "options_en": ["506.25%", "509.54%", "409.76%", "406.25%"], "options_hi": ["506.25%", "509.54%", "409.76%", "406.25%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let original radius = r</p><p>New radius = 225% of r = 2.25r</p><p>Original surface area = 4&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>New surface area = 4&#960;(2.25r)<sup>2</sup> = 4&#960;  X  5.0625 r<sup>2</sup></p><p>Increase = 5.0625 - 1 = 4.0625 </p><p>Percentage Increase = 4.0625  X  100 = 406.25%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let original radius = r</p><p>New radius = 225% of r = 2.25r</p><p>Original surface area = 4&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>New surface area = 4&#960;(2.25r)<sup>2</sup> = 4&#960;  X  5.0625 r<sup>2</sup></p><p>Increase = 5.0625 - 1 = 4.0625 </p><p>Percentage Increase = 4.0625  X  100 = 406.25%</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the volume of a sphere is 24,416.64 cm3, find its surface area (take &#960;=3.14) correct to two places of decimal.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; 24,416.64 cm3 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#960;=3.14 &#2354;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["3069.55 cm<sup>2</sup>", "4069.44 cm<sup>2</sup>", "5069.66 cm<sup>2</sup>", "6069.67 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["3069.55 cm<sup>2</sup>", "4069.44 cm<sup>2</sup>", "5069.66 cm<sup>2</sup>", "6069.67 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the radius of sphere = R</p><p>Volume of sphere = 24416.64</p><p><img width=120 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21889/image046.png\"></p><p><img width=81 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21889/image047.png\"></p><p>R = 18 cm</p><p>Surface area of the sphere = 4&#960;R<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 4 * 3.14 * 18<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 4069.44 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the radius of sphere = R</p><p>Volume of sphere = 24416.64</p><p><img width=120 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21889/image046.png\"></p><p><img width=81 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21889/image047.png\"></p><p>R = 18 cm</p><p>Surface area of the sphere = 4&#960;R<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 4 * 3.14 * 18<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 4069.44 cm<sup>2</sup></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the surface areas of two spheres are in the ratio of 9:49, then the ratio of their volumes is: (Where &#960; = 22/7)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9:49 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;: (&#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#960; = 22/7)</p>", "options_en": ["25:512", "49:363", "16:216", "27:343"], "options_hi": ["25:512", "49:363", "16:216", "27:343"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Surface area ratio = 4&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> / 4&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup> = (r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup> = 9/49</p><p>r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub> = 3/7</p><p>Volume ratio = (4/3)&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>3</sup>/(4/3)&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>3</sup> </p><p>= (r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub>)<sup>3</sup> </p><p>= (3/7)<sup>3</sup> </p><p>= 27/343</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Surface area ratio = 4&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> / 4&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup> = (r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup> = 9/49</p><p>r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub> = 3/7</p><p>Volume ratio = (4/3)&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>3</sup>/(4/3)&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>3</sup> </p><p>= (r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub>)<sup>3</sup> </p><p>= (3/7)<sup>3</sup> </p><p>= 27/343</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A copper sphere of diameter 18 metre is drawn into a cylindrical wire of length 12 metre. What is the radius of the wire?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>18 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2340;&#2366;&#2305;&#2348;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; 12 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2338;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["5 metre", "9 metre", "3 metre", "12 metre"], "options_hi": ["5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "9 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "3 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "12 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Diameter of sphere = 18m</p><p>Radius of sphere = 9m</p><p>Volume of sphere = <img width=16 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image035.png\">*&#960; r<sup>3</sup> =<img width=89 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image036.png\"></p><p>Height of cylindrical wire = 12m</p><p>Volume of cylindrical wire = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h = &#960; * r<sup>2</sup> * 12</p><p>&#960; * r<sup>2</sup> * 12 = <img width=89 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image036.png\"></p><p>r<sup>2</sup>= <img width=92 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image037.png\"></p><p>r = 9 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Diameter of sphere = 18m</p><p>Radius of sphere = 9m</p><p>Volume of sphere = <img width=16 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image035.png\">*&#960; r<sup>3</sup> =<img width=89 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image036.png\"></p><p>Height of cylindrical wire = 12m</p><p>Volume of cylindrical wire = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h = &#960; * r<sup>2</sup> * 12</p><p>&#960; * r<sup>2</sup> * 12 = <img width=89 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image036.png\"></p><p>r<sup>2</sup>= <img width=92 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20933/image037.png\"></p><p>r = 9 m</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the total surface area of a hemisphere with a radius of 11 cm?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["242&#960; cm<sup>2</sup>", "313&#960; cm<sup>2</sup>", "273&#960; cm<sup>2</sup>", "363&#960; cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["242&#960; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "313&#960; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "273&#960; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "363&#960; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Radius = 11 cm</p><p>Total surface area of a hemisphere = 3&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 3 * &#960; * 11 * 11</p><p>= 363&#960; cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Radius = 11 cm</p><p>Total surface area of a hemisphere = 3&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 3 * &#960; * 11 * 11</p><p>= 363&#960; cm<sup>2</sup></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Determine the total surface area of a hemisphere closed at bottom. Radius of the hemisphere is &radic;(25/&#960;) unit.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2306;&#2342; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &radic;(25/&#960;) &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["75 unit<sup>2</sup>", "70 unit<sup>2</sup>", "60 unit<sup>2</sup>", "50 unit<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["75 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;<sup>2</sup>", "70 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;<sup>2</sup>", "60 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;<sup>2</sup>", "50 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Total surface area of a hemisphere closed at bottom = 2&#960;r<sup>2</sup> + &#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 3&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 3 * &#960; * (&radic;(25/&#960;))<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 3 * &#960; * (25/&#960;)</p><p>= 75 unit<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total surface area of a hemisphere closed at bottom = 2&#960;r<sup>2</sup> + &#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 3&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 3 * &#960; * (&radic;(25/&#960;))<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 3 * &#960; * (25/&#960;)</p><p>= 75 unit<sup>2</sup></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the radius of a sphere is 2.1 cm, then the volume of sphere is equal to:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 2.1 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;:</p>", "options_en": ["36.088 cm<sup>3</sup>", "36.808 cm<sup>3</sup>", "38.808 cm<sup>3</sup>", "38.088 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["36.088 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "36.808 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "38.808 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "38.088 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Radius of sphere = 2.1 cm</p><p>Volume of sphere = 4/3 * 22/7 * 2.1<sup>3</sup> = 88 * 4.41 = 38.808 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Radius of sphere = 2.1 cm</p><p>Volume of sphere = 4/3 * 22/7 * 2.1<sup>3</sup> = 88 * 4.41 = 38.808 cm<sup>3</sup></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the surface area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of a sphere of diameter 28 cm. (Use &#960; = 22/7)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>28 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;2 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; (&#960; = 22/7 &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;)</p>", "options_en": ["1731", "2464", "2856", "1724"], "options_hi": ["1731", "2464", "2856", "1724"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Diameter = 28 cm</p><p>Radius r = 28/2 = 14 cm</p><p>Surface area of sphere = 4 * (22/7) * 14 * 14 = 88 * 28 = 2464 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Diameter = 28 cm</p><p>Radius r = 28/2 = 14 cm</p><p>Surface area of sphere = 4 * (22/7) * 14 * 14 = 88 * 28 = 2464 cm<sup>2</sup></p>"}]}